(SECTION 3: GENERATIVE AI SECURITY & INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY STANDARDS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.1 Safe Handling of Client Proprietary Data:) Tj
T*
(- Engineers must never paste unredacted client intellectual property, PII, or credentials into public LLM portals.) Tj
T*
(- Enterprise zero-data-retention APIs \(Google Cloud Vertex AI, Azure OpenAI, enterprise Gemini\) are approved.) Tj
T*
(- All documents indexed in vector databases \(such as ChromaDB\) must be purged upon project decommissioning.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.2 API Key Governance:) Tj
T*
(- API credentials \(including GEMINI_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, and TAVILY_API_KEY\) must strictly reside in local .env files.) Tj
T*
(- Hardcoding secrets or checking .env files into GitHub repositories is a critical security violation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.3 Verification & Hallucination Mitigation:) Tj
T*
(- Any production LLM workflow must implement context grounding and output validation \(e.g. Pydantic v2 schemas\).) Tj
T*
(- When a document Q&A assistant cannot find supporting facts in uploaded documents, it must explicitly state) Tj
T*
(  that the information was not found rather than hallucinating plausible answers.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
